{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_prediction_s86_item1_gauss_cut_gauss_constraint", "label": "Does the Gauss constraint cut the tent?", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The order's route claims the saturating tent violates Q non-decreasing and/or 1 <= Q <= Z, so intersecting the admissible set with those constraints would raise the threshold above K = 1.", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-S86-ITEM1-GAUSS-CUT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_s86_item1_gauss_cut_tent_admissible", "label": "The tent is Gauss-admissible \u2014 the route does not raise the threshold", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The tent's pieces are the tangent lines of S = uQ at u1 and u2, whose intercepts -u0^2 Q'(u0) are <= 0 wherever Q' >= 0; on such a line Q = b + alpha/u is non-decreasing, the pieces meet continuously, and Q_tent stays inside [Q(u1),Q(u2)] and hence inside [1,Z]. Both constraints are satisfied by the very object they were meant to exclude.", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-S86-ITEM1-GAUSS-CUT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_s86_item1_gauss_cut_sobolev_next_step", "label": "What would cut: finite kinetic energy, not Gauss", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A kink in S is a step in 4 pi r^2 rho, i.e. a jump in some P_nl: infinite kinetic energy. The constraint that excludes the saturating tent is P_nl in H^1 \u2014 a different mathematical language (Sobolev) \u2014 and it is named as the next step rather than measured here, per the standing protocol on nulls.", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-S86-ITEM1-GAUSS-CUT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_s86_item1_gauss_cut_canfail_suite", "label": "CF1-CF4: synthetic admissibility levers gating the 